# Spec §5.9 (Posponer), with §5.1–§5.5, §5.8 and §6.1 (checkbox).
# While now < pospuesta.hasta, a task that according to §5.1–§5.8 would be
# pending or overdue is waiting, with progress = (now − desde) /
# (hasta − desde). If it would be waiting by its own rule, the
# postponement changes nothing (status and progress of its rule). From hasta
# (inclusive), the status goes back to that of §5.1–§5.8: it can be overdue
# right away if its overdue moment arrived during the postponement. The postponement does not
# move due times or due dates.
# It can be completed while postponed: the checkbox is enabled
# unless the schedule prevents it (§5.5), and tapping it completes the task (a
# postponed task is not completed). Completing and undoing do not delete pospuesta.
# A paused task has no status even if it is postponed.
# "the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>" is tapping
# Posponer in the panel at that moment and choosing the option (1 hora, 3 horas or
# hasta mañana: 07:00 of the next day). Progress is a fraction
# between 0 and 1, compared exactly. When the step gives no creadaEn, the
# task was created before any other date of the scenario.
# U, V, N as in §5.2 and §5.3. Reference week: Monday 2026-07-13 to
# Sunday 2026-07-19.
Feature: Postponed task status

  # Postponed task status 1
  # A pending one-off task that is postponed is waiting, with the progress of the
  # postponement, up to the edge of hasta.
  Scenario Outline: Postponed task status 1
    Given a one-off task without a due date
    And the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>
    When I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is en espera
    And the progress is <progress>

    Examples:
      | option       | postponed           | now                 | progress |
      | 3 horas      | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 0        |
      | 3 horas      | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T10:45:00 | 0.25     |
      | 3 horas      | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T12:51:00 | 0.95     |
      | 1 hora       | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T10:30:00 | 0.5      |
      | hasta mañana | 2026-07-15T19:00:00 | 2026-07-16T01:00:00 | 0.5      |

  # Postponed task status 2
  # From hasta (inclusive), the one-off task is pending again.
  Scenario Outline: Postponed task status 2
    Given a one-off task without a due date
    And the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>
    When I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is pendiente

    Examples:
      | option       | postponed           | now                 |
      | 3 horas      | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T13:00:00 |
      | hasta mañana | 2026-07-15T19:00:00 | 2026-07-16T07:00:00 |
      | 1 hora       | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-16T10:00:00 |

  # Postponed task status 3
  # An overdue one-off task that is postponed is waiting (row 1). If its due
  # date passes during the postponement, it stays waiting (row 2).
  Scenario Outline: Postponed task status 3
    Given a one-off task with due date <due_date>
    And the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>
    When I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is en espera
    And the progress is <progress>

    Examples:
      | due_date   | option       | postponed           | now                 | progress |
      | 2026-07-14 | 3 horas      | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T11:30:00 | 0.5      |
      | 2026-07-15 | hasta mañana | 2026-07-15T19:00:00 | 2026-07-16T01:00:00 | 0.5      |

  # Postponed task status 4
  # When the postponement expires, the one-off task whose due date has already passed is
  # overdue right away (row 2: it passed during the postponement).
  Scenario Outline: Postponed task status 4
    Given a one-off task with due date <due_date>
    And the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>
    When I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is atrasada

    Examples:
      | due_date   | option       | postponed           | now                 |
      | 2026-07-14 | 3 horas      | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T13:00:00 |
      | 2026-07-15 | hasta mañana | 2026-07-15T19:00:00 | 2026-07-16T07:00:00 |

  # Postponed task status 5
  # A pending relative task that is postponed is waiting with the progress of the
  # postponement (row 1), also after its own overdue moment, V +
  # interval = 16:00 (row 2).
  Scenario Outline: Postponed task status 5
    Given a relative recurring task every <every> <unit>
    And the task was completed on <completed>
    And the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>
    When I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is en espera
    And the progress is <progress>

    Examples:
      | every | unit   | completed           | option  | postponed           | now                 | progress |
      | 4    | horas  | 2026-07-15T08:00:00 | 3 horas | 2026-07-15T12:30:00 | 2026-07-15T14:00:00 | 0.5      |
      | 4    | horas  | 2026-07-15T08:00:00 | 1 hora  | 2026-07-15T15:40:00 | 2026-07-15T16:10:00 | 0.5      |

  # Postponed task status 6
  # When the postponement expires before its overdue moment (16:00), the relative task goes
  # back to pending.
  Scenario Outline: Postponed task status 6
    Given a relative recurring task every <every> <unit>
    And the task was completed on <completed>
    And the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>
    When I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is pendiente

    Examples:
      | every | unit   | completed           | option  | postponed           | now                 |
      | 4    | horas  | 2026-07-15T08:00:00 | 3 horas | 2026-07-15T12:30:00 | 2026-07-15T15:30:00 |

  # Postponed task status 7
  # The postponement does not move the due time: the relative task becomes overdue at
  # 16:00 as if not postponed (row 1, not at 19:00), and if the overdue moment arrived
  # during the postponement, it is overdue right away on expiry (row 2).
  Scenario Outline: Postponed task status 7
    Given a relative recurring task every <every> <unit>
    And the task was completed on <completed>
    And the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>
    When I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is atrasada

    Examples:
      | every | unit   | completed           | option  | postponed           | now                 |
      | 4    | horas  | 2026-07-15T08:00:00 | 3 horas | 2026-07-15T12:30:00 | 2026-07-15T16:00:00 |
      | 4    | horas  | 2026-07-15T08:00:00 | 1 hora  | 2026-07-15T15:40:00 | 2026-07-15T16:40:00 |

  # Postponed task status 8
  # A pending weekly task (Tuesday 14) postponed until tomorrow stays
  # waiting past midnight, even though that day it would already be overdue.
  Scenario Outline: Postponed task status 8
    Given a weekly recurring task on <days> created on <created>
    And the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>
    When I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is en espera
    And the progress is <progress>

    Examples:
      | days           | created             | option       | postponed           | now                 | progress |
      | martes, jueves | 2026-07-13T08:00:00 | hasta mañana | 2026-07-14T19:00:00 | 2026-07-15T01:00:00 | 0.5      |

  # Postponed task status 9
  # On expiry, the weekly task that missed the Tuesday is overdue right away.
  Scenario Outline: Postponed task status 9
    Given a weekly recurring task on <days> created on <created>
    And the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>
    When I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is atrasada

    Examples:
      | days           | created             | option       | postponed           | now                 |
      | martes, jueves | 2026-07-13T08:00:00 | hasta mañana | 2026-07-14T19:00:00 | 2026-07-15T07:00:00 |

  # Postponed task status 10
  # Completing a postponed relative task: while it is waiting by its own
  # rule, its progress applies and not that of the postponement (row 1: V = 15:00,
  # progress (12:00 − 11:00) / 4 h). If its rule leaves it pending before
  # hasta, it is waiting with the progress of the postponement (row 2: V =
  # 11:30, progress (11:30 − 10:00) / 3 h).
  Scenario Outline: Postponed task status 10
    Given a relative recurring task every <every> <unit>
    And the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>
    When I complete the task on <completed>
    And I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is en espera
    And the progress is <progress>

    Examples:
      | every | unit   | option  | postponed           | completed           | now                 | progress |
      | 4    | horas  | 3 horas | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T11:00:00 | 2026-07-15T12:00:00 | 0.25     |
      | 1    | horas  | 3 horas | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T10:30:00 | 2026-07-15T11:30:00 | 0.5      |

  # Postponed task status 11
  # A postponed one-off task is completed by tapping the checkbox, and the postponement
  # stays stored.
  Scenario Outline: Postponed task status 11
    Given a one-off task without a due date
    And the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>
    When I tap the task checkbox on <tapped>
    Then the task is completed
    And the task is postponed from <from> to <to>

    Examples:
      | option  | postponed           | tapped              | from                | to                  |
      | 3 horas | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T10:30:00 | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T13:00:00 |

  # Postponed task status 12
  # Undoing the completion of a postponed one-off task returns it to waiting
  # by the postponement, which is still stored.
  Scenario Outline: Postponed task status 12
    Given a one-off task without a due date
    And the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>
    And the task was completed on <completed>
    When I delete the completion from <completed>
    And I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is en espera
    And the progress is <progress>
    And the task is postponed from <from> to <to>

    Examples:
      | option  | postponed           | completed           | now                 | progress | from                | to                  |
      | 3 horas | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T10:30:00 | 2026-07-15T11:30:00 | 0.5      | 2026-07-15T10:00:00 | 2026-07-15T13:00:00 |

  # Postponed task status 13
  # A postponed relative task with a completion from today is not completed:
  # tapping the checkbox completes it again (it does not delete today's completion).
  Scenario Outline: Postponed task status 13
    Given a relative recurring task every <every> <unit>
    And the task was completed on <completed>
    And the task was postponed with option <option> on <postponed>
    When I tap the task checkbox on <tapped>
    Then the task has two completions

    Examples:
      | every | unit   | completed           | option  | postponed           | tapped              |
      | 4    | horas  | 2026-07-15T08:00:00 | 3 horas | 2026-07-15T12:30:00 | 2026-07-15T13:00:00 |

  # Postponed task status 14
